6Head injuries
The following signs and symptoms  indicate a possible fracture of 
the skull or facial bones, concussion or compression:
• Deformed skull 
• Swollen, bruised or bleeding scalp
• Straw-coloured fluid or blood coming from the nose or 
ear(s)
• Bruising around the eyes (black eye) or behind the ears
• Nausea, vomiting, especially in children
• Confused, dazed, possibly combative
• Semi-conscious or unconscious
• Stopped breathing or irregular respiration
• Very slow pulse rate
• Pupils are of unequal size
• Pain at the injury site
• Weakened or paralyzed arms and/or legs
• Pain when swallowing or moving the jaw
• Wounds in the mouth
• Knocked-out teeth
• Shock
• Convulsions
An unconscious casualty with a head injury may vomit. Be ready 
to turn the casualty to the side (as a unit if possible) and clear the 
airway quickly.
192 193Bone and joint injuries
